.claude/
CLAUDE.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
node_modules/
.venv/

# builder-generated artifact (cleaned requirements written into a project's opt/)
opt/_requirements.builder.txt

# The reference study's generated assets: 15 MB rebuilt by make_reference_study.py
# on demand. Anchored, because unanchored this matched every assets/ in the tree
# -- including the scaffold's, whose .gitkeep files survive only by predating the
# rule. A new asset directory there was invisible to `git status` and to
# `git add`, which for a directory that gets copied into every new study is a
# study missing a folder it was supposed to have.
/examples/reference/assets/
# setuptools' wheel scratch. `python -m build` leaves a whole second copy of
# every package under build/lib -- the builder's static files included -- so a
# grep finds every hit twice and the second one is stale.
build/

# Build artefacts. `pip install -e .` -- which the README instructs -- rewrites
# these on every run, and a permanently dirty tree trains people to ignore
# `git status`, which is how an accidental `git add -A` sweeps something in.
*.egg-info/

# The built documentation site. `mkdocs build` writes 6 MB here, most of it
# copies of the walkthrough screenshots; the published copy is the gh-pages
# branch that `mike deploy` writes, never this.
/site/
